## A First Look at R and RStudio
### Part 1 — Set up your workspace

***1. Create a class folder.***
***2. Make an easy-to-find folder (e.g., SOC205A or Stats_Class) where you’ll save all course files.***
***3. Install the software: R (the programming language) and then RStudio (the IDE for working in R).***
***4. Follow your course links or search “Install R” and “Install RStudio” (Desktop/Free). Install R first, then RStudio.***
***5. Start RStudio & (strongly recommended) create a Project.***
***6. Go to File ▸ New Project ▸ New Directory ▸ New Project, name it (e.g., lecture-1), and choose your class folder.***
***6. Working in a Project keeps your paths, files, and knitting nice and tidy.***
***7. Sanity check: In the R console, type version$version.string and press Enter. You should see a version line (e.g., “R version 4.x.x”).***

### Part 2 — Set up  R Markdown

***1.In RStudio, go to the top menu and choose.***
***2.ile ▸ New File ▸ R Markdown…***
***3.A dialog box will appear. Fill it out as follows.***
***4.Title: Lecture 1 Practice.***
***6Author: Your name***
